        "original_id": "f9cb2f7b-231c-5469-a393-cb724319bb41",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Saipan, Battle of Stones River\n- Places: Saipan, Mariana Islands, Middle Tennessee\n- Wars and campaigns: Pacific campaign of World War II, Stones River Campaign, Western Theater of the American Civil War\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Stones River, also called the Second Battle of Murfreesboro, was fought in Middle Tennessee from December 31, 1862, to January 2, 1863.\n- The Battle of Stones River was the culmination of the Stones River Campaign in the Western Theater of the American Civil War.\n- The Battle of Saipan was fought on the island of Saipan in the Mariana Islands from 15 June to 9 July 1944.\n- The Battle of Saipan was a battle of the Pacific campaign of World War II.",
